{"name":"Chatroom","hex":"#b0ab9c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chatroom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of chat room."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chatroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chatroom (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Chatroom is a 2010 British psychological thriller drama film directed by Hideo Nakata from a screenplay by Enda Walsh, based on Walsh's 2005 play of the same name. The film follows five teenagers who meet on an online chatroom and encourage each other's bad behaviour."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a7/Chatroom_%28film%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatroom_(film)","wikidata":"Q1068272"},{"title":"Online chat","blocks":[{"text":"Online chat is any direct text-, audio- or video-based (webcams), one-on-one or one-to-many (group) chat, using tools such as instant messengers, Internet Relay Chat (IRC), talkers and possibly MUDs or other online games. Online chat includes web-based applications that allow communication – often directly addressed, but anonymous between users in a multi-user environment. Web conferencing is a more specific online service that is often sold as a service, hosted on a web server controlled by the vendor. Online chat may address point-to-point communications as well as multicast communications from one sender to multiple receivers and voice and video chat, or may be a feature of a web conferencing service."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Gossip-chat.png/330px-Gossip-chat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Online_chat","wikidata":"Q287198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Colloquy.png/500px-Colloquy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","s